# Search

::summary
The universal search CONTENT — everything that renders inside the search modal (`modals/search.surf` owns the frame; this file owns the states): the shell-context wrapper carrying the default open state (raised from Docs), the Find ⇄ Ask segmented-control, the seven-scope single-select segmented-control with per-surface pre-selection (WP-N3 08-11 — the toggled-button chip row died with the inline filter rows), and the six reviewed states — open-from-Docs recents, Everything recents, Find results, Find no-match, Ask idle, Ask answered. Recents and hits route exactly alike: click routes to the item's surface and closes the sheet.
::

Search is NOT a routed surface — shipped, it mounts inside `::modal[name=search]`, a centered sheet floated over the raising surface (top 64px, `min(640px, 100vw − 20px)` wide). The wrapper below is the shell-composition stand-in the static engine can express: the sheet body centered in the main pane over the Docs context that raised it.

## State 1 in shell context — open from Docs (scope-aware recents, RULED 08-05)

Input autofocused and empty, Docs chip pre-selected, Recents already populated and filtered to the Docs scope.

